{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-13786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}5{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-13786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=-4x,$ then, \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4\\,⟹\\,-\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}5{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{u}(-\\frac{1}{4})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{-4})}{e}^{u}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}({e}^{u}){|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{-4})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{-4})}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}({3}^{-4}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}(\\frac{1}{{3}^{4}}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}(\\frac{1}{81}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}(-\\frac{80}{81}) \\\\  & =\\frac{100}{81}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-13786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a93a13ab8920d4c479a654cadb38091cd27efcfa00ea8668b199227c098f0bf7"} {"question" "q-13786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-13786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{100}{81}"] ["math" "\\frac{100}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{10}{27}"] ["math" "\\frac{40}{81}"] ["math" "\\frac{80}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-13786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{100}{81}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-349601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}4{e}^{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-349601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=4x+1,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $9$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4{e}^{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{1}^{9}{e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{9}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\,{|}_{1}^{9} \\\\  & ={e}^{9}-{e}^{1} \\\\  & ={e}^{9}-e\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-349601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a93a13ab8920d4c479a654cadb38091cd27efcfa00ea8668b199227c098f0bf7"} {"question" "q-349601" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-349601" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^9-e"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-113833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int {e}^{x/2\\,-\\,1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-113833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=\\frac{x}{2}-1,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,2\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{x/2\\,-\\,1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{u}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\,{e}^{u}+C \\\\  & =2\\,{e}^{x/2\\,-\\,1}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-113833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a93a13ab8920d4c479a654cadb38091cd27efcfa00ea8668b199227c098f0bf7"} {"question" "q-113833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-113833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\,{e}^{x/2\\,-\\,1}+C"] ["math" "2\\,{e}^{x-1}+C"] ["math" "2\\,{e}^{x/2\\,-\\,1}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{x/2\\,-\\,1}}{2}+C"] ["math" "{e}^{x/2\\,-\\,1}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-113833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\,{e}^{x/2\\,-\\,1}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-13732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int 5{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-13732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=3x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5{e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{u}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{3x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-13732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a93a13ab8920d4c479a654cadb38091cd27efcfa00ea8668b199227c098f0bf7"} {"question" "q-13732" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-13732" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{e}^{3x}+C"] ["math" "5{e}^{3x}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}{e}^{3x}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{3x}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{5x}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-13732" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{3x}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-51160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int {e}^{z}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-51160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{z}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z=\\int {e}^{2z}\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nIf we let $u=2z$, then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}z}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}z=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{2z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int {e}^{2z}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2z}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {e}^{u}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2z}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-51160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a93a13ab8920d4c479a654cadb38091cd27efcfa00ea8668b199227c098f0bf7"} {"question" "q-51160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-51160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{{e}^{{z}^{2}}}{2}+C"] ["math" "2{e}^{2z}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2z}}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{z}}{2}+C"] ["math" "{e}^{2z}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-51160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{2z}}{2}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-349646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}{5}^{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-349646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=x-1,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{5}^{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{5}^{u}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\,{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}({5}^{1}-{5}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(5-\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-349646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a93a13ab8920d4c479a654cadb38091cd27efcfa00ea8668b199227c098f0bf7"} {"question" "q-349646" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-349646" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{24}{5\\ln(5)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-31417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int {6}^{x/3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-31417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=\\frac{x}{3},$ then,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {6}^{x/3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {6}^{u}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int {6}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\frac{{6}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot {6}^{x/3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-31417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a93a13ab8920d4c479a654cadb38091cd27efcfa00ea8668b199227c098f0bf7"} {"question" "q-31417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-31417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3\\cdot {6}^{x/3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\cdot {6}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{6}^{x/3}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{6}^{x/3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{6}^{x}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-31417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\cdot {6}^{x/3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-31413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int {4}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-31413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=5x$, then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {4}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {4}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int {4}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\frac{{4}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{5x}}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-31413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a93a13ab8920d4c479a654cadb38091cd27efcfa00ea8668b199227c098f0bf7"} {"question" "q-31413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-31413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{{4}^{5x-7}}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{4}^{5x}}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{4}^{5x}}{5}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{4}^{5x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{4}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-31413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{4}^{5x}}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-30973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-30973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=6x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $6$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of  $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}{3}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{6}{3}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{{3}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}){|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(729-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{728}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =\\frac{364}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-30973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a93a13ab8920d4c479a654cadb38091cd27efcfa00ea8668b199227c098f0bf7"} {"question" "q-30973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-30973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{121}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "\\frac{364}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "\\frac{364}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{364}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "\\frac{728}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-30973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{364}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-349631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\cdot {4}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-349631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=1-x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1\\,⟹\\,-\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\cdot {4}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{0}2\\cdot {4}^{u}(-1)\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{0}{4}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{{4}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}){|}_{1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}({4}^{0}-{4}^{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(1-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-349631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a93a13ab8920d4c479a654cadb38091cd27efcfa00ea8668b199227c098f0bf7"} {"question" "q-349631" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "q-349631" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{6}{\\ln(4)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/state.json" "file_sha256" "c15a3658413aa6017c0c53bb53d9f561307e92a72bc1e156205aa12c4c6fd90f"} {"question" "e-459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate  $\\displaystyle{\\int e^{1-3x}\\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/example-459.json" "file_sha256" "2d4876ba083fff19532693ea4c70afb24dfe9d6c82ce7a7f60711a984783bebf"} {"question" "e-459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=1-3x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = -\\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{1-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{u}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{u}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{1-3x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/example-459.json" "file_sha256" "2d4876ba083fff19532693ea4c70afb24dfe9d6c82ce7a7f60711a984783bebf"} {"question" "e-460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate  $\\displaystyle{\\int 3^{5+4x}\\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/example-460.json" "file_sha256" "fcabefe314d7eeb8c3e35d4fdc3c6cdb21027b71e004fff3ea88ec5f70b99f3e"} {"question" "e-460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=5+4x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 4\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = \\dfrac 1 4 \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {3}^{5+4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {3}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {3}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{{3}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{5+4x}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/example-460.json" "file_sha256" "fcabefe314d7eeb8c3e35d4fdc3c6cdb21027b71e004fff3ea88ec5f70b99f3e"}] "usage" {"e-460" [] "e-459" []} "basis" 1125 "retractions" [[17592186096377 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\displaystyle \\int e^{1-3x}\\, \\textrm{d}x}$."] [17592186096377 :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=1-3x$, then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = -\\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\inte^{1 - 3x}dx &= \\inte^{u} \\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}\\inte^{u}du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}e^{u} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}e^{1 - 3x} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096378 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\displaystyle \\int 3^{5+4x}\\, \\textrm{d}x}$."] [17592186096378 :question/worked-solution "If we let\n\n$$\nu=5+4x\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 4\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = \\dfrac 1 4 \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int3^{5 + 4x}dx &= \\int3^{u} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}\\int3^{u}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{3^{u}}{\\ln 3} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{3^{5 + 4x}}{4\\ln 3} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
